			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Enforce explicit function qualification in IPC command handlers\n\nUpdate Tauri command handlers in `Source/Binary/IPC/` to replace direct module function calls with the explicit `::Fn()` qualification pattern (e.g., `mountain_get_cache_stats::mountain_get_cache_stats`). Apply the same pattern to struct initialization (`CollaborationPermissions::Struct`), aligning with the project's ongoing modularization effort and strict PascalCase naming conventions.\n\nThis change prevents potential symbol shadowing issues within the `IPC::AdvancedFeatures` and `IPC::StatusReporter` modules, ensuring consistent symbol resolution across the binary initialization and command handling architecture. It maintains architectural consistency with recent refactorings in `PublishNotification`, `CommandProvider`, and `Entry` modules.",
